    "recommendations": "• Mark the single access point with a clearly visible address sign readable from the approaching roadway.\n• Post a site map showing the locations of all three buildings at the access point entrance to orient arriving responders.\n• Mark the internal drive aisle with directional signage to guide responders to each building.\n• Keep the internal drive aisle clear of parked vehicles to maintain continuous movement between structures.\n• Identify and mark a designated staging area within the vehicle parking area for emergency vehicles.\n• Mark the secondary and detached buildings with individual unit or building identifiers visible from the drive aisle.\n• Identify and mark the rear of the main building to alert responders to limited rear access conditions.\n• Keep the service area clear of stored materials that would block responder access along that side of the property.\n• Mark walkways connecting buildings so responders can move between structures on foot without confusion.\n• Confirm rooftop access points for all three buildings are labeled at ground level near each structure's entrance."
